{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"printf '\\\\n--- venue ---\\\\n'; cat VENUE.md; printf '\\\\n--- strategy relevant sections ---\\\\n'; rg -n 'Supplement|LLM|source_ids|prior_paper|edit_framing|staged_input|5.5|9in' paper_strategy.md paper_strategy.json; printf '\\\\n--- style geometry ---\\\\n'; rg -n 'textwidth|textheight|twocolumn|columnsep|oddsidemargin' paper.sty; printf '\\\\n--- local scripts ---\\\\n'; rg --files .codex | sort; printf '\\\\n--- edit inputs ---\\\\n'; ls -ld previous_paper aggregated extra_tasks 2>/dev/null; printf '\\\\n--- workspace metadata ---\\\\n'; cat .agentic_paper_workspace.json; printf '\\\\n--- memory tail ---\\\\n'; tail -25 memory.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"printf '\\\\n--- venue ---\\\\n'; cat VENUE.md; printf '\\\\n--- strategy relevant sections ---\\\\n'; rg -n 'Supplement|LLM|source_ids|prior_paper|edit_framing|staged_input|5.5|9in' paper_strategy.md paper_strategy.json; printf '\\\\n--- style geometry ---\\\\n'; rg -n 'textwidth|textheight|twocolumn|columnsep|oddsidemargin' paper.sty; printf '\\\\n--- local scripts ---\\\\n'; rg --files .codex | sort; printf '\\\\n--- edit inputs ---\\\\n'; ls -ld previous_paper aggregated extra_tasks 2>/dev/null; printf '\\\\n--- workspace metadata ---\\\\n'; cat .agentic_paper_workspace.json; printf '\\\\n--- memory tail ---\\\\n'; tail -25 memory.md\"","aggregated_output":"\n--- venue ---\n# ICLR 2026 Venue Brief\n\nUse this brief to tailor the manuscript for the International Conference on Learning\nRepresentations 2026 submission.\n\n## Hard Constraints\n- Target venue: ICLR 2026.\n- Submission type: conference paper.\n- Body-page budget: 8 to 9 pages, excluding references. A body of 8 pages counts only when its final page is at least 75% full; a shorter or sparser body fails validation.\n- Review model: double-blind. The submission must be fully anonymized.\n- Omit author names, affiliations, acknowledgements, and funding statements from the manuscript.\n- Do not include self-identifying links such as personal repositories, lab pages, or internal URLs.\n- Refer to your own prior work in the third person; never write phrasing that reveals authorship.\n- Include a separate `LLM Usage` section, which may appear in the appendix, describing the precise role\n  of LLMs in research ideation and writing. Significant LLM use must be disclosed; nondisclosure can\n  cause desk rejection.\n- The paper must satisfy the ICLR template and formatting rules selected by `--paper-format iclr`.\n\n## Audience\n- Machine learning researchers working on representation learning, optimization, architectures, and\n  empirical methodology.\n- Readers expect a clearly stated contribution, honest baselines, controlled comparisons, ablations\n  that isolate the mechanism, and explicit statements of scope and limitations.\n- Reviewers reward reproducibility and calibrated claims far more than headline numbers.\n\n## Framing Priorities\n- Lead with the research question and the specific claim the evidence supports.\n- State the contribution precisely in the abstract and introduction: what is new, what it improves,\n  and under which conditions.\n- Motivate the method mechanistically. Explain why it should work, not only that it does.\n- Support the central claim with controlled comparisons against meaningful baselines.\n- Use ablations to attribute the gain to the proposed component rather than to incidental changes.\n- Report variance across seeds or runs whenever the artifacts provide it.\n- Be explicit about the regime studied and where the result is not expected to hold.\n\n## Manuscript Guidance\n- Prefer a title and abstract that name the mechanism and the setting, not a generic improvement claim.\n- In the introduction, make the contribution list concrete and verifiable against the artifacts.\n- In the method section, give enough detail to reimplement: objective, architecture, and the\n  hyperparameters that matter.\n- In the results section, foreground controlled comparisons, ablations, sensitivity, and failure modes.\n- Include a limitations discussion that a reviewer would otherwise raise.\n- Figures must meet top-tier conference standards in both design (clean typography, consistent colors,\n  proper labels and legends, high resolution) and scientific content (clear message, no filler).\n- The template is single-column: size figures for the full text width and keep axis labels legible.\n\n## Anti-Goals\n- Do not deanonymize the submission in any way.\n- Do not overclaim generality beyond the settings actually evaluated.\n- Do not present a benchmark delta as a mechanistic insight without evidence connecting the two.\n- Do not omit baselines or ablations that the grounded artifacts already support.\n- Do not describe results as state of the art unless the comparison in the artifacts establishes it.\n- Do not pad the paper to fill the page budget.\n\n## Decision Rule\n- When venue framing and grounded evidence conflict, follow the grounded evidence.\n- Use this brief to choose emphasis, terminology, and narrative framing, not to invent stronger claims\n  than the run supports.\n\n--- strategy relevant sections ---\npaper_strategy.json:8:  \"prior_paper_story_status\": \"recentered\",\npaper_strategy.json:9:  \"edit_framing_decision\": \"This is a fresh framing, not a manuscript-edit run: no resolved edit-context files, previous_paper, aggregated, extra_tasks, or contributions scaffold is present. Recentered denotes moving from the source task's broad accuracy agenda to the supported endpoint-regression comparison and its limitations; it does not assert that a prior manuscript was revised. Preserving a hypothetical prior story would invent evidence. Broadening to a shared estimator/architecture family is unsupported. Centering the completed final comparison is preferable to either broadening or a development-improvement narrative.\",\npaper_strategy.json:10:  \"staged_input_impact\": [\npaper_strategy.json:64:      \"layout_rationale\": \"The inspected paper.sty is single-column, with 5.5in text width and 9in text height; column width equals full text width, not a 2.6in double-column slot. Target 5.39in width by about 1.7-1.9in height, with caption occupying about one quarter page in total. Place on page 1 or 2. Use one cohesive panel with at most three horizontal zones, at most six short conceptual labels, no tiny equations, and rendered text at least 8.5pt. All-treated/all-control are prediction inputs, not observed outcome labels. Use an editable draw.io source, not invented empirical curves; the task's graph sketch is explicitly schematic.\",\npaper_strategy.json:81:      \"layout_rationale\": \"Use a 2-by-2 grid over the inspected 5.5in single text column, about 3.8-4.2in high plus a concise caption, roughly half a body page. Each approximately 2.6in-wide panel has six horizontal condition rows and three dodged comparator markers, a shared logarithmic ratio axis, and a vertical reference at one; use one shared three-entry legend. Labels such as No spill, Weak linear, Strong linear, Threshold, Two-hop, and Cluster are defined in the protocol table. Render labels at least 8.5pt, markers clearly separated, and at most two panels per row. Compute ratios of per-cell RMSEs, not means of per-seed ratios. Seed-block bootstrap intervals are planned summaries, not currently supplied estimates; do not attach significance stars. Report absolute errors beside this figure in a main-text table.\",\npaper_strategy.json:98:      \"layout_rationale\": \"Use two panels in one row across the inspected 5.5in single-column text width, approximately 2.4-2.7in high plus caption, about one third page. Panel A uses transparent points and three semantic groups, not six colored mechanism series; show all scientific records and no fitted causal trend. Its observations are seed-dependent and are not independent sample-size evidence. Panel B has four graph categories and two design series with seed-block uncertainty, not four overlapping method curves. Keep labels at least 8.5pt and use the same condition names as Figure 2. If crowding occurs, stack the two panels and revise the page allocation rather than shrinking text; all support-fraction tables remain in the supplement.\",\npaper_strategy.json:111:        \"source_ids\": [\"final.evidence.episodes\", \"final.metric.mean_capped_normalized_rmse\", \"final.metric.mean_absolute_capped_normalized_bias\"]\npaper_strategy.json:116:        \"source_ids\": [\"final.evidence.episodes\"]\npaper_strategy.json:121:        \"source_ids\": [\"result.best_correct_score\", \"final.evidence.episodes\"]\npaper_strategy.json:126:        \"source_ids\": [\"final.evidence.episodes\", \"final.qualification.status\", \"final.qualification.outcome\"]\npaper_strategy.json:131:        \"source_ids\": [\"final.qualification.status\", \"final.qualification.outcome\", \"final.qualification.correct\", \"final.metric.control_success_fraction\", \"final.metric.failed_episode_fraction\", \"final.evidence.episodes\"]\npaper_strategy.json:134:        \"heading\": \"LLM Usage\",\npaper_strategy.json:135:        \"grounded_content\": \"Include the venue-required separate section disclosing documented LLM roles in ideation, candidate-code generation, reference-query planning, framing, writing, and figure preparation as applicable. Use actual process artifacts under results/ideas and the local strategy/agent records; distinguish work already performed from future writing/figure activity. These process artifacts, not scientific metric source IDs, ground the disclosure. Include no author identities, personal links, funding, or acknowledgements.\",\npaper_strategy.json:136:        \"source_ids\": []\npaper_strategy.json:175:    \"ICLR 2026 is fixed by VENUE.md: anonymized conference submission, 8-9 body pages excluding references; an eight-page body must finish at least 75% full. No names, affiliations, acknowledgements, funding, self-identifying repositories, or internal URLs. Include a separate LLM Usage section, preferably after references. The supplied paper.sty confirms single-column 5.5in by 9in geometry; its historical header does not independently verify official 2026 template provenance. Check official-template provenance during final preparation and regenerate figures if geometry differs, rather than silently treating this as a double-column format.\",\npaper_strategy.md:93:`VENUE.md` fixes ICLR 2026 and an 8-9-page body excluding references. The inspected `paper.sty` specifies a **single text column, 5.5 inches wide and 9 inches high**. Here column width equals full text width; there is no double-column half-width slot. Use full-width figures rather than shrinking dense panels into imagined narrow columns. The style's historical header is not independent proof of official 2026 release provenance; verify that during final preparation and regenerate assets if geometry changes.\npaper_strategy.md:100:| `conditional_accuracy` | Required matplotlib 2×2 dot-whisker comparison; each family has six condition rows and three ratios, selected RMSE divided by baseline RMSE | Full 5.5 in width, about 3.8-4.2 in high; two panels per row; six categories, three series per panel; shared log ratio axis and line at one; shared three-entry legend | Main results; roughly half page |\npaper_strategy.md:137:## Supplementary Information After References\npaper_strategy.md:146:6. **LLM Usage.** A separate venue-required section disclosing the precise documented roles of LLMs in ideation, code generation, query planning, framing, and eventual writing/figure work. Use actual process artifacts under `results/ideas/` and local planning records, not performance source IDs or assumptions. Disclose performed activity separately from work still planned, without identifying authors.\npaper_strategy.md:156:The ICLR 2026 manuscript must be fully anonymous: no names, affiliations, acknowledgements, funding, self-identifying links, or internal URLs. Include the separate `LLM Usage` section after references if appropriate. Current readiness applies to framing only, not verified official-template provenance, citation completeness, completed plot assets, uncertainty computations, or compiled-page compliance.\n\n--- style geometry ---\n40:\\oddsidemargin .5in    %   Note \\oddsidemargin = \\evensidemargin\n48:\\textheight 9.0 true in       % Height of text (including footnotes & figures)\n49:\\textwidth 5.5 true in        % Width of text line.\n83:\\def\\@maketitle{\\vbox{\\hsize\\textwidth\n215:\\textheight=#5\\vbadness=10000\\vfuzz=120ex\\overfullrule=0pt%\n216:\\global\\setbox\\iclrrulerbox=\\vbox to \\textheight{%\n217:{\\parskip=0pt\\hfuzz=150em\\cv@boxheight=\\textheight\n229:\\def\\iclrruler#1{\\makevruler[12pt][#1][1][3][0.993\\textheight]\\usebox{\\iclrrulerbox}}\n232:\\iclrruleroffset=\\textheight\n245:% \\colorbox[rgb]{0.7,0.7,0.7}{\\small \\parbox[b][\\textheight]{0.1cm}{}}}\n\n--- local scripts ---\n.codex/skills/generate-concept-figure/SKILL.md\n.codex/skills/memory-log/SKILL.md\n.codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py\n.codex/skills/retrieve-references/SKILL.md\n.codex/skills/retrieve-references/scripts/openalex_fetch.py\n.codex/skills/retrieve-references/scripts/s2_fetch.py\n.codex/skills/retrieve-references/scripts/scholarly_fetch.py\n.codex/skills/retrieve-references/templates/provenance.schema.json\n.codex/skills/scientific-evidence/SKILL.md\n.codex/skills/scientific-evidence/scripts/scientific_evidence.py\n.codex/skills/scientific-evidence/scripts/scientific_evidence.sh\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/SKILL.md\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/compile_latex.sh\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_compile_inputs.py\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_figures.py\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_rendered_si.py\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_tex_refs.py\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/templates/figure_manifest.schema.json\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/SKILL.md\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/scripts/validate_claims.py\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/alife/alifeconf.sty\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/alife/paper.tex\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/claims_grounding.schema.json\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/iclr/paper.bst\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/iclr/paper.sty\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/iclr/paper.tex\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/references.bib\n\n--- edit inputs ---\n\n--- workspace metadata ---\n{\n  \"global_memory_dir\": \"work/results/t09/codex/20261107_014043/investigation\",\n  \"output_dir\": \"work/results/t09/codex/20261107_014043/paper\",\n  \"results_dir\": \"work/results/t09/codex/20261107_014043/investigation\",\n  \"schema_version\": 1,\n  \"task_dir\": \"work/results/t09/codex/20261107_014043/task\"\n}\n\n--- memory tail ---\n\n### 2026-11-07T03:37:33.157966+00:00 | step=paper | scope=paper\n- summary: Framing audit independently confirmed completed qualified final evaluation and no edit-mode inputs; favor conditional endpoint-regression accuracy over search improvement.\n- evidence: final.qualification.status=completed; final.qualification.outcome=qualified; final.evidence.episodes contains 24 seeds, 576 scientific cases and 48 matched controls. downstream_study and study.* sources absent; ablation_studies empty. ICLR single-column paper.sty specifies 5.5in text width and 9in text height. No previous_paper, aggregated, extra_tasks or resolved edit context exists.\n- next_action: Reaggregate existing final records and inspect the selected estimator and benchmark mechanisms; choose a thesis and figures that retain regressions, dependence and missing ablations.\n- tags: gate=kept, trigger=none, reason=Framing audit adds no new experiment and does not alter research recommendations\n\n### 2026-11-07T03:37:46.968344+00:00 | step=paper | scope=paper\n- summary: Select a conditional endpoint-regression comparison, not a search-success narrative; confirmed final qualification independently and inspected template geometry.\n- evidence: final.qualification.status=completed and final.qualification.outcome=qualified. final.evidence.episodes contains 24 seeds and 576 scientific cases; study.* sources and edit inputs absent; ablation_studies empty. paper.sty has 5.5in single-column text width and 9in text height. Memory helper initially rejected global_memory symlink; resolved physical paths preserve append-only logging.\n- next_action: Compute concis